step	44	-	Quick guide step 44
line	<str>Talk to Lokar Searunner on the western most Rellekka docks. D*K*S closest fairy ring.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Brundt the Chieftain in the Longhall for a Seal of Passage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Lokar Searunner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb the ladders, and board the pirate ship. Talk to Captain Bentley about sailing to Lunar Isle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Captain Bentley again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the nearby south stairs through the door, talk to 'Birds-Eye' Jack.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb back up the stairs and talk to Captain Bentley again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb back down the stairs and return to 'Birds-Eye' Jack again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to 'Eagle-eye' Shultz at the very front (north-end deckside) of the ship.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Cabin boy up one deck from the captain (south).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to 'Beefy' Burns on the lowest level of the ship.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to 'Lecherous' Lee at the very top-rear of the ship.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to First mate 'Davey-boy', on the deck level, south room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb back up to the top, talk to the Cabin boy (2 inventory spaces required).</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the emerald lens on the bullseye lantern you brought. Light it with your tinderbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the lantern on the following objects, and rub away the symbols:</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Bentley.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the ladders and walk into the city (there will be a small cut-scene).</str>
line	
line	<str>Run out of the city to the south-east part of the island. Talk to the Oneiromancer.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill Suqah (safespottable), until you've received a suqah tooth. Keep any hides you get as drops (you will need a total of 4 hides later in the quest, which you can also collect later).</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the city, northern section. Enter the chicken house and talk to Baba Yaga (1 inventory space required).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the house and use the vial on a nearby water source.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the Oneiromancer with the potion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your Dramen staff/staves on the following altars in order:</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel back to Lunar Isle and give the Lunar staff to the Oneiromancer. Do not forget to bring your Seal of Passage.</str>
line	
line	<str>In the north-eastern part of the isle, climb down ladder to the Lunar Mine.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine a stalagmite for 1 lunar ore. Grab three extra ores to save time during The Fremennik Exiles quest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Smelt the ore at a furnace or superheat the ore to receive a lunar bar (closest furnace and anvil is in Rellekka).</str>
line	
line	<str>With a hammer, use the bar on an anvil to make the helm.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to the Lunar Isle.</str>
line	
line	<str>North-west in the city, talk to Pauline Polaris (1 inventory space required) Note: The chat options appear in a random order when guessing her real name. First guess must be Pauline. Pick the option that says "Jane Blud-Hagic-Maid."</str>
line	
line	<str>South in the city, talk to Meteora.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill Suqahs until one drops a special tiara. Keep up to 4 hides the Suqahs drop. Make sure you have at least 4 hides.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give Meteora the tiara.</str>
line	
line	<str>South of the bank, talk to Rimae Sirsalis about ceremonial clothes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Rimae Sirsalis again, she will tan your hides.</str>
line	
line	<str>Craft a Lunar torso, trousers, gloves and boots from your hides.</str>
line	
line	<str>Centre of the city, talk to Selene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the city and run south then west past the two bridges. With your spade, dig up the blue flowers furthest west to receive the lunar ring. (You must click continue on the chatbox!)</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the Oneiromancer all your lunar gear. She will then give you all the items back. You will need to have 11 inventory spaces free (8 for your lunar gear and 3 other spaces) or you cannot continue.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Waking sleep vial on the kindling you received.</str>
line	
line	<str>Get your combat runes and supplies and wear all your lunar items (but do NOT bank your Seal of Passage). 4 inventory spaces are required.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter a long building on the western side of the village that has a ceremonial brazier and a staircase inside.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Light the ceremonial brazier then use the kindling on it.</col>
